<title>USA: First Defiance sets new share buyback.</title>
<headline>First Defiance sets new share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>DEFIANCE, Ohio 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Defiance Financial Corp said Wednesday it planned to buy back up to 471,168 shares, which is 5.0 percent of its outstanding common stock.</p>
<p>The repurchase plan will be in effect for one year, beginning June 2, the company said.</p>
<p>The company said that in January, it completed the repurchase of 495,596 common shares at $11.674 a share.</p>
<p>It was the third repurchase it had undertaken in 12 months, during which it reacquired 1,566,211 shares, it said.</p>
<p>First Defiance is the holding company for First Federal Savings and Loan of Defiance, Ohio.</p>
